       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1000 mg of sertraline once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious toxicity. It may be a typo for 100 mg.\n\nTypical adult dosing:\n- **Starting dose:** 25\u201350 mg by mouth once daily. Depending on the indication, this is often 50 mg for depression and 25 mg for panic disorder or PTSD.\n- **Titration:** Increase in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of at least one week.\n- **Usual range:** 50\u2013200 mg once daily.\n\nTell me the dose you want, such as 50 mg or 100 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 1000 mg, please confirm that with your supervising resident or attending and with pharmacy first."
