     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 1000 mg/day is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I don't see a clinical scenario where it would be safe. A medical student confirming it isn't enough to change that, because the confirmation doesn't address the safety problem.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If it was a typo,** give me the intended dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg once daily, and I'll enter it now.\n- **If you think a dose above 200 mg is needed,** discuss it with your supervising resident or attending and with pharmacy. If they approve it, they can enter or co-sign the order through the proper channels.\n- **If you're worried about a possible overdose or ingestion,** contact poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) and your team right away. That is a different situation from writing a prescription.\n\nI can help you work out a starting dose and titration plan for the indication you're treating."
      }
     ],
